# Bona marketing integrations — copy to ~/.secrets/bona-marketing.env (mode 0600).
#
# install.sh copies this file there when it is missing. Every key is optional: an
# empty value switches that integration OFF (no fan-out, no probe), so the services
# start fine before any account exists. Read only inside Node (services/api/lib/env.mjs);
# never cat, echo or commit the real file. Fill each value from the checklist named
# beside it, then run:  node scripts/marketing/verify-integrations.mjs
#
# Public ids that the BROWSER needs (GA4 measurement id, Meta pixel id, Snap pixel id,
# Search Console tag) live in src/data/site.json → analytics, not here.

# ---- Meta (docs/checklists/meta-bona-portfolio.md) --------------------------------
# Events Manager › Data sources › dataset "Bona web" › the Dataset ID (formerly Pixel ID),
# 15–16 digits. The same number goes into site.json → analytics.metaPixel.
META_PIXEL_ID=
# Events Manager › the dataset › Settings › Conversions API › "Generate access token"
# (a System User token scoped to the dataset). Starts with EAA…
META_CAPI_TOKEN=
# Events Manager › the dataset › "Test events" tab › the code shown there (TEST12345).
# Leave empty once events show up as "Received" — a test code diverts them out of
# reporting.
META_TEST_EVENT_CODE=

# ---- Google Analytics 4 (docs/checklists/google-bona.md) ---------------------------
# Admin › Data streams › the web stream › Measurement ID (G-XXXXXXXXXX). Mirrors
# site.json → analytics.ga4; the server needs it to address the Measurement Protocol.
GA4_MEASUREMENT_ID=
# Admin › Data streams › the web stream › "Measurement Protocol API secrets" › Create.
GA4_API_SECRET=

# ---- Snapchat (docs/checklists/snapchat-bona.md) -----------------------------------
# Snap Ads Manager › Events Manager › the Snap Pixel › Pixel ID (a UUID). Mirrors
# site.json → analytics.snapPixel.
SNAP_PIXEL_ID=
# Snap Ads Manager › Business Details › "Conversions API tokens" › Generate.
SNAP_CAPI_TOKEN=
